      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T18:21:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "USB-IF Type-C R2.0 spec dictates devices /must/ detect a disconnect within tPDDebounce (10-20ms) to remain compliant with spec. More preferably faster.\n\nUSB-IF TCPCI R2.0 v1.2 spec dictates tCCStatusDelay update limits for functional TCPCI implementations. This is indirectly capped by higher protocol limits like tRpValueChange for sub-state transitions.\n\nA USB-C compliant device should be able to abide by the lower bound of tErrorRecovery. May I ask how and why this 500ms value is being derived? I feel the DUT failing tests is indicative of a problem that needs to be resolved with the DUT -- not something to be mitigated by altering (arguably) spec-compliant Servo.",
      "parentUuid": "05902746_a6ad8982",
